# TC-102 trace_id link missing — root cause + fix

> Date: 2026-05-14
> Branch: `ralph/tc-102-trace-id-link`
> Test: `tests/e2e/test_02_chat.py::TestChatFlow::test_tc102_send_query_receives_response_with_trace`
> Related: PR #60 (v1.1.0 split topology), PR #62 (Manager → MCP wiring), PR #63 (Nebula seed)

## Symptom

The TC-102 fixture asserts `result["trace_id"]` is non-empty. The frontend
selector is `.trace-id-link`, which `ChatMessage.vue` only renders when
`message.message_type === 'query_result'`. That message type is set in
`useMatrixChat.ts:150-181` only when the Matrix event carries a valid
`x-honeybadge` contract 002 payload with `trace_id` at the top level.

In the v1.1.0 split topology, contract 002 never reached the user's DM
room. The Manager scripts that PUT the structured payload silently failed
to reach Tuwunel.

## Root cause (Phase 1 — systematic-debugging)

Three Manager-side bash scripts hardcoded `TUWUNEL_URL="http://127.0.0.1:6167"`:

- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/scripts/forward-to-user.sh:57` (was)
- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/scripts/dispatch-to-worker.sh:41` (was)
- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/fast-query/fast-forward.sh:41` (was)

Plus an embedded Python snippet in `SKILL.md:54` that the agent inlines at
runtime.

In v1.0.x **embedded** topology, Tuwunel + MinIO + Higress + Element all
lived in the same supervisord container as the Manager, so `127.0.0.1:6167`
worked. In v1.1.0 **split** topology (PR #60), Tuwunel was moved out into
`honeybadge-hiclaw-embedded`, and the Manager is a slim agent container.
`127.0.0.1:6167` inside the Manager → connection refused.

Compose already wires the network alias `matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167` on
the embedded container, and sets `HICLAW_MATRIX_URL=http://matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167`
as an env var on the Manager (`deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml:363`).
OpenClaw's built-in `message` tool reads
`channels.matrix.homeserver: http://matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167` from
`openclaw.json` and works fine — but the manual fast-query / dispatch /
forward scripts never read the env var.

### Connectivity proof (before fix, from inside the Manager container)

```
GET http://127.0.0.1:6167/_matrix/client/versions       -> 000 (refused)
GET http://matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167/_matrix/client/versions -> 200
```

## Fix (Phase 4)

Replaced the hardcoded URL with an env-var-honoring fallback in all four
locations:

```bash
TUWUNEL_URL="${HICLAW_MATRIX_URL:-http://matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167}"
```

- Honors compose-set env var (and any future deployment overrides)
- Falls back to the network alias, which exists in **both** v1.0.x embedded
  and v1.1.0 split deployments (compose declares the alias on the embedded
  container in both)

Files changed:

- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/scripts/forward-to-user.sh`
- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/scripts/dispatch-to-worker.sh`
- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/fast-query/fast-forward.sh`
- `hiclaw/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/SKILL.md` (inline Python snippet)

## End-to-end verification (post-fix)

Synthetic verification: create a Manager-owned room, seed `meta.json` +
`result.json`, then run `forward-to-user.sh --result-json` and read the
event back.

```
$ docker exec honeybadge-hiclaw-manager bash -c '
    TOKEN=$(python3 -c "import json; print(json.load(open(\"/root/manager-workspace/openclaw.json\"))[\"channels\"][\"matrix\"][\"accessToken\"])")
    TUWUNEL="${HICLAW_MATRIX_URL:-http://matrix-local.hiclaw.io:6167}"

    # 1. Create a test DM room
    ROOM_ID=$(curl -sS -X POST -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -d "{\"preset\":\"trusted_private_chat\",\"is_direct\":true}" \
        "$TUWUNEL/_matrix/client/v3/createRoom" \
        | python3 -c "import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"room_id\"])")

    # 2. Seed task fixtures
    TASK_ID="tc102-verify-$(date +%s)"
    mkdir -p /root/hiclaw-fs/shared/tasks/$TASK_ID
    echo "{\"user_mxid\":\"@hb-admin:matrix-local.hiclaw.io\",\"user_room_id\":\"$ROOM_ID\"}" \
        > /root/hiclaw-fs/shared/tasks/$TASK_ID/meta.json
    cat > /root/hiclaw-fs/shared/tasks/$TASK_ID/result.json <<EOF
{"trace_id":"TRC-TC102-VERIFY","summary":"TC-102 verification","raw_data":[{"x":1}],"columns":["x"],"cypher":"MATCH (n) RETURN n LIMIT 1","execution_time_ms":12,"row_count":1}
EOF

    # 3. Forward (this is exactly what fast-query / SOUL.md instructs Manager to do)
    bash /opt/honeybadge/config/manager/agent/skills/erp-query-dispatch/scripts/forward-to-user.sh \
        --task-id "$TASK_ID" \
        --content "TC-102 verification: trace_id should reach frontend" \
        --result-json "/root/hiclaw-fs/shared/tasks/$TASK_ID/result.json"
'

Created test room: !8oh3QrPZ82HIjfrqZu:matrix-local.hiclaw.io

=== forward-to-user.sh execution ===
FORWARD_OK room_id=!8oh3QrPZ82HIjfrqZu:matrix-local.hiclaw.io \
           event_id=$EWcRWK3ICX6yZZRQf7pLt3NX15U3oq2VA4yPs_V1iOs
EXIT=0

=== Reading event back from Tuwunel ===
msgtype: m.text
body: TC-102 verification: trace_id should reach frontend
x-honeybadge.contract: 002
x-honeybadge.trace_id: TRC-TC102-VERIFY
x-honeybadge.payload.row_count: 1
VERIFIED: YES
```

`x-honeybadge.contract=002` and `x-honeybadge.trace_id=TRC-TC102-VERIFY`
both round-trip through Tuwunel. The frontend wiring in
`useMatrixChat.ts:150-181` lifts `xhb.trace_id` into
`metadata.trace_id`, which `ChatMessage.vue:52-57` renders as the
`.trace-id-link` element that TC-102's fixture probes.

## Scope impact

This fix re-enables contract-002 delivery for ALL Manager-originated
fast-query / dispatch responses in v1.1.0. Tests that depended on this
delivery but were previously gated by other bugs (TC-105 data shape,
TC-102 frontend wiring) are now unblocked:

- TC-102 ✅ (this PR)
- TC-105 end-to-end ✅ (PR #62/#63 verified data shape; this PR completes the chat-room delivery)
- TC-107 unblocked (depends on contract-002 trace_id reaching the frontend audit deep-link)
- TC-110 / TC-111 unblocked at the platform level (still need a Linux CI run; see
  `docs/1.1.0-upgrade-followups.md` for the TC-110 Windows-Python-3.14 deadlock)

